On Tue, Apr 06, 2004 at 08:35:14PM -0500, Art Haas wrote:
> Hi.
> 
> Like the subject stated, I'm looking for sparc assembly language
> references. My goal is to be able to read and understand a good bit of
> the various '.S' files used in the sparc port. I downloaded a number of
> PDF files from Sun - one is an assembly language reference, another is
> the V8 manual. Using these two documents I've been able to make sense of
> some of the files, but there is stil much to learn. What other materials
> do people on the list recommend?

I read "A Laboratory Manual for the SPARC". It's college class material,
and was really useful. Even points to the isem, which is a sparc
emulator, just enough to run sparc-a.out code.

